sangati rashi

  -- rashi: a measurable quantity — the thing being measured.
  -- the general form of which mass, velocity, force, energy etc. are all particulars.
  --
  -- a rashi has three aspects:
  --   sankhya  — the numeric value (how much)
  --   matra    — the unit (in what terms)
  --   vishesa  — the type (which quantity: mass, velocity, ...)
  --
  -- a named quantity instance (v1, m1, a) is a rashi:
  --   [v1, vishesa, velocity]   -- specific type
  --   [v1, vishesa, rashi]      -- general: v1 is a measurable quantity
  --   [v1, sankhya, "20.0"]     -- value
  --   [v1, matra,   metre-per-second]  -- unit
  --
  -- distinct from the kosha concept (velocity) which is the universal —
  -- rashi is the particular instance that appears in a specific question.
  -- the kosha concept is atemporal; rashi is situated in a problem context.

  "pramana-swarupa sankhya-yukta matra-yukta"
  "vishesa-sthita sambandha-yukta"
  "prashna-sthita viveka-kriya"

shabda rashi / a-measurable-quantity-instance-situated-in-a-problem-context

done
